		c	Example 1: <pre>\n     {@code mcSection.addEntry((mc, isExtended) -> Optional.of("test"));}\n This will add the string 'test' to the entries of the section {@code mcSection}.\n </pre>\n <br> <br>\n Example 2: <pre>\n {@code mcSection.addEntry((mc, isExtended) -> {\n String username = mc.thePlayer.username;\n\n if(isExtended) {\n    return Optional.of(username);\n }\n else {\n    return Optional.empty();\n }});}\n This will add the username of the player to the section {@code mcSection} if {@code isExtended} is {@code true}\n and if {@code false}, will return an empty {@code Optional} which result in no text added to the section.\n </pre>
	m	(Lapi/client/debug/IDebugInfoProvider;I)V	addEntryWithIndex	addEntryWithIndex	addEntryWithIndex
		c	Example 1: <pre>\n     {@code mcSection.addEntryWithIndex((mc, isExtendedDebug) -> Optional.of("test"), 3);}\n This will add the string 'test' at the 4th line of the section {@code mcSection} and move next lines by 1 (starts at 0).\n </pre>\n <br> <br>\n Example 2: <pre>\n {@code mcSection.addEntryWithIndex((mc, isExtended) -> {\n String username = mc.thePlayer.username;\n\n if(isExtended) {\n    return Optional.of(username);\n }\n else {\n    return Optional.empty();\n }}, 3);}\n This will add the username of the player at the 4th line of the section {@code mcSection} if {@code isExtended} is {@code true}\n and if {@code false}, will return an empty {@code Optional} which result in no text added to the section.\n </pre>
	m	(I)V	removeEntry	removeEntry	removeEntry
		c	Example: <pre>\n     {@code mcSection.removeEntry(1);}\n This will remove the second entry of {@code mcSection} (start at 0).\n </pre>
